# Never upload local environment files to a Vercel build.
#
# `vercel deploy` uploads the working directory, and .gitignore does not gate
# that upload. Without this, a local .env is bundled into the deployment and
# Next.js loads it on the server — so AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000 wins over
# the platform's own configuration, Auth.js decides the connection is insecure,
# issues a non-Secure session cookie, and middleware then rejects every request.
#
# Environment configuration belongs in the Vercel project, never in the upload.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local-only artifacts
.next
node_modules
.git
scripts/_tmp-*
